# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings on every system, so the gate's carriage-return rule
# and the tests' byte counts mean the same thing on Windows, Linux and macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf
# A Windows batch file needs CRLF, so it is stored with CRLF and never converted: what a checkout or an archive gives is
# byte for byte what git stores, which Anthropic's plugin directory requires to validate the repository.
*.cmd -text
